Z||000000||Avery Montembeault||02-12-2001||04:25 PM||||My bro reccently got an 88 pontiac grand am with a stock 4 banger and as he was driving, the engine basically blew up into little bitty pieces. When he took it into my uncles auto shop, my uncle basically laughed his ass off over what a piece of crap my bro was driving. Then when he was informed that I reccently got an 88 fiero, he laughed even harder. Apperently he knows something I do not. Any ideas as to what Ive gotten myself into?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hank is Here||02-12-2001||04:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Avery Montembeault:<BR><B> Any ideas as to what Ive gotten myself into?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hopefully a good car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Welcome to the Forum.  An 88' Fiero is like any other 88' car on the road today, it is 13 years old so it will have its quirks.  Some people just give the Fiero a bad wrap without reason, ask you uncle what his reason is.  88's have a different suspention so finding some parts is not easy.  other than that it all comes down to how the car was maintained before you got it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GT||02-12-2001||05:33 PM||||I have learned since becoming a fiero owner that you get some goofy looks or stupid comments whenever you tell somebody you have a fiero.. The most common comments are, "Death Trap", "Dont they blow up when rear ended?", and "I didnt think those were still around."  These people that have said these things dont know a lick of what there talking about either.  ||||reg||1
